\[
\xymatrix{\mathrm{Spc}(q^*)\colon \mathrm{Spc}(\mathrm{Mod}_{\mathrm{Sp}_{E}}^c(\underline{R/p}_E)) \ar[r] & \mathrm{Spc}(\mathrm{Mod}_{\mathrm{Sp}_{E}}^c(\underline{R}_E))}
\]

Let $\mathbb{T} = (S^{1})^{\times r}$ be a torus of rank $r$ and view $E \subset \mathbb{T}$ via the embedding of the $p$-th roots of unity. By naturality, the reduction map $q\colon R\to R/p$ fits into a commutative square of graded commutative cohomology rings:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:lem:injectivity1}
\vcenter{
\xymatrix{H^*(E;R) \ar[d] & H^*(\mathbb{T};R) \ar[l] \ar[d] \\
H^*(E;R/p) & H^*(\mathbb{T};R/p). \ar[l] }
}
\end{equation}
First, we claim that the bottom horizontal map is an $F$-isomorphism. Indeed, the proof of \cref{lem:groupcohomologybasechange} shows that $H^*(\mathbb{T};R/p) \to H^*(E;R/p)$ identifies with
\[
H^*(\mathbb{T};\mathbb{F}_p) \otimes_{\mathbb{F}_p} R/p   \to H^*(E;\mathbb{F}_p) \otimes_{\mathbb{F}_p} R/p,
\]
base-changed from the $F$-isomorphism $H^*(\mathbb{T};\mathbb{F}_p) \to H^*(E;\mathbb{F}_p)$. This implies the claim. Second, the right vertical map in \eqref{eq:lem:injectivity1} may be identified with the projection
\[
R[y_1,\ldots,y_r] \to R/p[y_1,\ldots,y_r]
\]
with $|y_i| = -2$ for all $i$. Applying homogeneous Zariski spectra to the square \eqref{eq:lem:injectivity1} thus yields a commutative diagam
\begin{equation}\label{eq:lem:injectivity2}
    \xymatrix{\mathrm{Spec}^h(H^*(E;R)) \ar[r] & \mathrm{Spec}^h(H^*(\mathbb{T};R)) \\
